---
// Scene tab: the full pipeline from workflows/wf.json.
// The selects that depend on the Python catalogue (/api/options) are filled at
// runtime by src/scripts/scene.ts, exactly as before, so the page and
// scripts/*.py cannot drift apart.
---

<main id="view-scene">
  <form class="panel" id="scene-form">
    <label for="prompt">Prompt</label>
    <textarea id="prompt" required>quick, no upscale</textarea>

    <label for="negative">Negative <span class="hint">(blank = workflow default)</span></label>
    <textarea id="negative" style="min-height:52px"></textarea>

    <div id="init-block">
      <label for="init_file">Start from an image <span class="hint">(blank = from noise)</span></label>
      <div id="init-drop" class="init-drop">
        <input id="init_file" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" hidden />
        <img id="init-preview" alt="init image" hidden />
        <div id="init-placeholder">Drop an image here, or <button type="button" id="init-pick" class="linkish">choose a file</button></div>
        <button type="button" id="init-clear" class="secondary" hidden>Remove</button>
      </div>
      <p class="note" id="init-status" hidden></p>
      <div id="denoise-cell" hidden>
        <label for="denoise">Denoise <span class="hint">(how much gets repainted)</span></label>
        <div class="row">
          <input id="denoise" type="range" min="0.05" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.6" />
          <output id="denoise-out">0.60</output>
        </div>
        <p class="note">The sampler skips the first <code>steps × (1 − denoise)</code>
        of the schedule, so the input survives in inverse proportion. Around
        0.3 it is a retouch, 0.6 a reinterpretation, 1.0 ignores the image
        entirely and you are back to text2img. The face pass and the upscale
        run after this, unchanged.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="family">Model</label>
        <select id="family">
          <option value="wai">WAI Illustrious (SDXL)</option>
          <option value="anima">Anima Aesthetic (2B DiT)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div id="lora-cell">
        <label for="lora">Style LoRA <span class="hint">(0 = off)</span></label>
        <input id="lora" type="number" step="0.05" min="0" max="1.5" value="0.5" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" id="family-note"></p>

    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="width">Width</label><input id="width" type="number" value="1024" step="64" min="256" /></div>
      <div><label for="height">Height</label><input id="height" type="number" value="1024" step="64" min="256" /></div>
    </div>

    <div id="pose-block" hidden>
      <div class="check"><input id="pose_on" type="checkbox" /><label for="pose_on">Pose control <span class="hint">(skeleton, Anima only)</span></label></div>
      <div id="pose-editor" hidden>
        <div class="row">
          <div><label for="pose_preset">Template</label><select id="pose_preset"></select></div>
          <div><label>&nbsp;</label><button type="button" class="secondary" id="pose-reset">Reset</button></div>
        </div>
        <canvas id="pose-canvas" class="pose-canvas"></canvas>
        <p class="note" id="pose-hint"></p>
        <div class="row">
          <div><label for="pose_style">Skeleton style</label><select id="pose_style"></select></div>
          <div><label for="pose_strength">Strength <span class="hint">(0-2)</span></label><input id="pose_strength" type="number" step="0.05" min="0" max="2" value="1" /></div>
        </div>
        <p class="note">R2_puppet followed arm angles within ~13° up to 60° above horizontal; an arm straight up tends to flip the figure to a back view. Strength above 1 measured worse. Naming the pose in the prompt helps.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="steps">Steps</label><input id="steps" type="number" value="20" min="1" /></div>
      <div><label for="cfg">CFG</label><input id="cfg" type="number" step="0.5" placeholder="default" /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="seed">Seed <span class="hint">(blank = random)</span></label><input id="seed" type="number" placeholder="random" /></div>
      <div><label for="batch">Batch</label><input id="batch" type="number" value="1" min="1" max="8" /></div>
    </div>

    <label for="remove_bg">Background removal</label>
    <select id="remove_bg"></select>

    <div class="check"><input id="no_upscale" type="checkbox" checked /><label for="no_upscale">Skip upscale (faster, ~18 s)</label></div>
    <div class="check"><input id="no_face" type="checkbox" /><label for="no_face">Skip face pass (FaceDetailer)</label></div>

    <details id="face-tuning">
      <summary>Face pass prompt</summary>
      <label for="detail_prompt">Positive <span class="hint">(blank = workflow default)</span></label>
      <textarea id="detail_prompt" style="min-height:52px"></textarea>
      <label for="detail_negative">Negative</label>
      <textarea id="detail_negative" style="min-height:52px"></textarea>
      <p class="note">FaceDetailer resamples inside the face mask with
      <b>this</b> prompt, not the one above, so whatever it names wins there.
      The shipped default is
      <code id="detail-default">&hellip;</code> &mdash; note it fixes eye colour
      and will override the scene prompt's. Ignored when the face pass is
      skipped.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Background tuning</summary>
      <div class="check"><input id="bg_refine" type="checkbox" /><label for="bg_refine">Refine the mask edge</label></div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="bg_sensitivity">Sensitivity</label><input id="bg_sensitivity" type="number" step="0.05" value="1.0" /></div>
        <div><label for="bg_blur">Mask blur</label><input id="bg_blur" type="number" value="0" min="0" /></div>
      </div>
      <label for="bg_offset">Mask offset <span class="hint">(negative shrinks)</span></label>
      <input id="bg_offset" type="number" value="0" />
      <p class="note">Only used when a removal model is selected. The node reads
      every optional input without <code>.get()</code>, so all four are always sent.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Request limits</summary>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="cost">Cost units</label><input id="cost" type="number" value="100" min="1" /></div>
        <div><label for="timeout">Timeout (s)</label><input id="timeout" type="number" value="900" min="30" /></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">A cold start is ~7 min. Below ~600 s the request can time
      out while the machine is still booting.</p>
    </details>

    <div class="row">
      <button id="scene-go" type="submit">Generate</button>
      <button id="scene-cancel" type="button" class="secondary" hidden>Cancel</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Full scene pipeline from <code>workflows/wf.json</code>:
    collage, detail pass, FaceDetailer, optional upscale.</p>
  </form>

  <section>
    <div class="panel">
      <div id="scene-progress"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="scene-empty" class="empty" style="margin-top:16px">
      Nothing rendered yet in this session.
    </div>
    <div id="scene-gallery" class="gallery"></div>
  </section>
</main>
